1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT My Heritage: https://www.myheritage.se/dna/match-theory/D-55ED2D48-00D7-4121-BFAD-273A465A1B64-D-CED20C24-075F-4F9B-BC13-1EE5F5F26751-S-FFMC-CFFFM?utm_content=theories_email&email_check=1&utm_campaign=500296&tr_date=20190911
2 CONT
2 CONT Embias Records:  shows  the family departed Hjeltan Torp  31 Jan. 1903
2 CONT
2 CONT Ellis Island Records:  family arrived 17 March 1903 on the ship Ivernia from Liverpool, England
2 CONT
2 CONT They were joining an uncle, Johan M Engblom born 1867.  He was Jonas mother's brother
2 CONT
2 CONT The Mattsons  became naturalized citizens in 1909
2 CONT
2 CONT They purchased land and owned a farm in Isanti County Minnesota.  They lived in that general area until their passing.
2 CONT
2 CONT Note:  Ingrid and Jonas changed their last name upon entering the U.S.  Changed it to Mattson taken from the name of his father Jöns Mattson.  MeriKay told me they changed it because there were too many Jonssons. (uppgift Julia Ba
2 CONC cklund Arnold)
2 CONT
2 CONT Enligt Ewa Johnson, Anbytarforum, gifter sig Ingrid Katarina med Jonas Jönsson f. 1865 Torp. "De bor enl. Folkräkningen 1900 i Hejltan 1 Torp och har barnen Lydia Katarina f. 1894 Torp, Jöns Olof f 1896 Torp och Per Mathias f. 189
2 CONC 9 Torp. Selina Matilda finns då hos dem som piga." Selina var Ingas syster, vilken också emigrerade.
2 CONT
2 CONT Uppgifter från Julia Backlund Arnold: I will now relate Anna and Jonas emigrating
2 CONT
2 CONT You know of her marriage to Jonas August Backlund as well as the birth of 2 sons.  The dates are on the family tree I will send.
2 CONT
2 CONT They left from Trondhjem, Norway and were to arrive Ellis Island July 27, 1903.  When they arrived in England  for the 2nd leg of their journey Johan Algot (oldest son) was deemed sick and they would not allow him to board the shi
2 CONC p  So, the family returned home and rebooked their passage.  Only this time they traveled with only the youngest son Olaf Albin who was 7 months. Arriving at the Port of Quebec  Aug. 22, 1903.  Their destination was the home of An
2 CONC nas' sister and brother in law Inga (Ingrid Katarina)and Jonas Matson in Albert Lea, Minnesota. They left sick Johan with his Backlund grandmother in Stode and Johan did not come to the states until he could pay his own passage.  
2 CONC  Arriving  Oct. 18, 1920 when he was 19.  Story is he never forgave his father for abandoning and not sending for him.  I assume they never had the money.
