1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Charles/Carl Hjalmar in Sweden was a Funiture Carpenter; in United states he also was a House Builder
2 CONT
2 CONT House shown in  U.S. National Register of Historic Places; built by Wiksell: http://www.waymarking.com/waymarks/WMKR6M_Bedard_House_Thompson_Falls_MT
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------
2 CONT Carl H. Wicksell, died Sunday morning. Funeral rites were conducted yesterday.  Charesl H. Wicksell was born February 17, 1882, at farm Krokain Söderåkra, landscape Småland, Kalmar Län, Sweden. He moved to the US when he was 20. D
2 CONC uring the year 1907, he was married to Salena M. Lindgren in Isanti, Minnesota. Salena( later also Lena) was born in Borgsjö parish in Medelpad, Västernorrland County in Sweden.
2 CONT
2 CONT They later moved to Thompson Falls, Montana, where their only child, Carl, Jr., was born in 1915. They resided there until 1925 at which time the family moved to Chelan. Surviving are his wife, Salena; his son, Carl Jr., one broth
2 CONC er, Robert and three sisters, Signe, Constance and Annette residing in Sweden; one cousin, Otto Hendrickson, Bryn Marr, Wa., and nephew, J. O. Matson of Chelan.
2 CONT
2 CONT (Information from http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GSln=Wicksell&GSbyrel=in&GSdyrel=in&GSob=n&GRid=24194834&  Washington Death Certificate and private sources) Name Carl Hjalmar Wicksell Death date 08 Sep 1940 Deat
2 CONC h place Chelan, Chelan, Washington
2 CONT
2 CONT Age at death 58 years 6 months 21 days Estimated birth year 1882 Marital status Married Spouse name Lena M. Wicksell Father name Nils Johnson Mother name Annalisa Bergstrom Film number 2023753 Digital GS number 4222935 Image numbe
2 CONC r 532 Reference number cn 101
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
