1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Marker: The Worst Aircraft Disaster in Georgia History Location: Acworth Dallas Highway across from New Hope Baptist Church in New Hope Cemetery (Side 1)
2 CONT
2 CONT April 4, 1977 The Worst Aircraft Disaster in Georgia History
2 CONT
2 CONT On April 4, 1977 a DC-9 Southern Airways Flight 242 flying from Huntsville, AL to Atlanta encountered a dangerous thunderstorm over Rome, GA. The hail and rain the aircraft endured was so severe that both engines flamed out and th
2 CONC e aircraft quickly lost altitude. The flight crew desperately attempted to land the DC-9 on GA 92 Spur, now known as GA 381 which runs through the community of New Hope.
2 CONT
2 CONT The result was the worst aircraft disaster in GA history claiming 72 lives including 9 local residents of New Hope. Miraculously 22 passengers survived.
2 CONT
2 CONT New Hope Fatalities
2 CONT
2 CONT Kathy Griffin Carter and son Jeffrey Richard Carter Faye Robinson Griffin and son Larry Allen Griffin Edna Griffin Gamel, son John T. Gamel and daughter Courtney A. Gamel Berlie Mae Bell Craton Ernest L. Prewett
2 CONT
2 CONT New Hope Memorial 
2 CONT
2 CONT NORTHWEST ARKANSAS TIMES     21 Aug 1944 Om fadern och familj 3 articles appear in the Northwest Arkansas Times Newspaper about Carl E Wicksell.   He is a pianist and entertained the troops at the USO.     Some time after the 1940
2 CONC  Federal Census Carl and family along with Celina (following the death of her husband) move to Arkansas.   The birthplace of Carl's wife Dorothy.   A son Larry Wicksell   is born 19 May 1941 Wenatchee, Washington A son Byron Wicks
2 CONC ell   is born 11 March 1944 Arkansas
2 CONT
2 CONT WICKSELL, BYRON was born 11 March 1944, received Social Security number 263-64-1617 (indicating Florida) and, Death Master File says, died April 1977   4,587,978  More resources: 
2 CONT
