1 OCCU Curate, temporary Assisstant Vicar, Rätan Parish, Härjedalen, Jämtland, Sweden (2005 photo Rätan kyrka - church)
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Born 26 July 1784 Asen, Liden Parish, Sweden (Liden ka C:1) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Attended Härnosänd Grammer School 1802-1805 (Upper Secondary School or Senior High School) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Registered 12 November 1805 at University of Uppsala, Sweden (Uppsala University Matr lV – rolls of students part 4)
2 CONT
2 CONT Ordained 1808 (Bucht: Härnosänd Gymnasiematrikel 1800-1849 page 4, rolls of students edited by Gösta Bucht)
2 CONT
2 CONT Curate, temporary Assistant Vicar in Rätan Parish. The vicar (kyrkoherde) was the superior and had assistants (komminister) and curates (pastorsadjunkt) to help with the services in the annex churches and chapels. Rätan was an ann
2 CONC ex parish to Berg.
2 CONT
2 CONT Died of neurasthenia 2 August 1826 in Assistant Vicar’s house, Rätan Parish, Sweden, Buried 17 September 1826 in Rättan Parish (Rätan Kyrkoarkiv C:2 page 204)
2 CONT
2 CONT The symptoms of Neurasthenia are fatigue, anxiety, neuralgia (painful disorder of cranial nerves - excruciating pain, usually on one side of the face and muscle spasms "suicide disease") and depression. Today this is sometimes dia
2 CONC gnosed as fibromyalgia or chronic fatigue syndrome.
