1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Source ===
2 CONT MH:S500034  Sweden Household Examination Books, 1860-1930  MyHeritage  Each book or series of books represents a 3-10 year period of time within a parish. Every year until 1894 the Parish Priest would visit each home and test each
2 CONC  individual's knowledge of the catechism.They would also collect information about birth dates, marriages, deaths, where people had moved to or from, etc. Each year the priest would come back and update the information of the prev
2 CONC ious year,noting changes within the population of the home. After 1894 the examinations were less focused on doctrinal knowledge and more focused on enumerating the Swedish population.MyHeritage has produced an every-name index to
2 CONC  nearly 8 million images provided by our Swedish partner ArkivDigital. This portion of the Swedish Household Examination Books (Husförhörslängder), mostly covers the years 1860-1930, with some few exceptions from the early 1800's 
2 CONC and late 1700's. The Examination books are an invaluable collection that can provide insight into the make-up of families within Sweden, from birth to death or emigration. Because the books were updated every year, families can be
2 CONC  traced year to year, and often from location to location throughout the country. Until 1894 the Parish Priest wouldvisit each farm or home within his Parish in order to grade and document each individuals understanding of the cat
2 CONC echism. After 1894 the Examinations Books were replaced by Församlingsbok, records of the Church of Sweden which were used to officially enumerate the population from year to year, but the focus on examining the knowledge of the c
2 CONC atechism had been removed.  10180  Collection MH:SC7174  https://www.myheritage.com/research/record-10180-110651888/tage-aron-in-sweden-household-examination-books  https://www.myheritage.com/research/record-10180-110651888/tage-a
