1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Emigrerade 1896-05-23 till Nordamerika. Flyttar till USA nr 15(1)
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT According to John A Sandstrom's draft card, he was 40 years old at the time of signing the draft card. The "description of registrant" indicates that John A. was of medium build, blue eyes and had dark brown hair. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was employed by Highland Paint & Wall Co located on 140 State St in Springfield, MA as a painter. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs.Signe Sandstrom was listed as his wife at the time of signing the draft card on Sept 1, 1918. They lived on 578 Central St. in Springfield, MA.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to the 15th Census of the United States completed in 1930 for the area of Springfield City, Massachusetts, County of Hampden (census taker's name was Mary C. Hough), John A. Sandstrom's year of immigrationg to the U.S. f
2 CONC rom Sweden was 1896. His native tongue was Swedish but he also could speak English. Rundhill was listed as John's wife. She was 40 years old at the time of the census. Her year of immigration was 1912, also from Sweden. Her native
2 CONC  tongue was Swedish, but also could speak English. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Carl and Albert were listed as sons of John A. and Rundhill, they were each 16 years old at the time of the 1930 U.S. census.  It appears that they lived on Harer St. - (street name was difficult to read clearly.) Their home was v
2 CONC alued at approximatly $2,000
2 CONT * '''Residence''': 1920 - Precinct A Part Of Springfield City 7 Part Of, Hampden, Massachusetts, USA
2 CONT * '''Immigration''': 1896
